# 02 - Implementation Guide

Follow the phases in order. The complete finished configuration is in [`configs/BR1-SW01.cfg`](../configs/BR1-SW01.cfg); this guide shows how it is built and verified step by step.

## Phase 0 - Console access and factory reset

1. Connect the USB-to-RJ45 console cable from **PC-A** to the switch console port.
2. Open Device Manager, note the COM port (e.g. `COM3`).
3. Open PuTTY / Tera Term: **Serial**, that COM port, **9600 baud, 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit, flow control None**.
4. Reset to a clean state:

```
Switch> enable
Switch# write erase
Switch# delete flash:vlan.dat
Switch# reload
```

Answer `confirm` to each prompt. After boot, decline the initial configuration dialog (`no`).

5. Record the platform details for your documentation:

```
Switch# show version
Switch# show inventory
```

## Phase 1 - Base device configuration

```
Switch> enable
Switch# configure terminal
Switch(config)# hostname BR1-SW01
BR1-SW01(config)# no ip domain-lookup
BR1-SW01(config)# ip domain-name lab.local
BR1-SW01(config)# clock timezone SAST 2 0
BR1-SW01(config)# service password-encryption
BR1-SW01(config)# enable secret <YOUR_ENABLE_SECRET>
BR1-SW01(config)# username netadmin privilege 15 secret <YOUR_ADMIN_SECRET>
BR1-SW01(config)# login block-for 120 attempts 3 within 60
BR1-SW01(config)# vtp mode transparent
```

## Phase 2 - VLANs, STP and errdisable recovery

```
BR1-SW01(config)# vlan 10
BR1-SW01(config-vlan)# name STAFF
BR1-SW01(config-vlan)# vlan 20
BR1-SW01(config-vlan)# name GUEST
BR1-SW01(config-vlan)# vlan 99
BR1-SW01(config-vlan)# name MANAGEMENT
BR1-SW01(config-vlan)# vlan 999
BR1-SW01(config-vlan)# name BLACKHOLE
BR1-SW01(config-vlan)# exit
BR1-SW01(config)# spanning-tree mode rapid-pvst
BR1-SW01(config)# spanning-tree portfast default
BR1-SW01(config)# spanning-tree portfast bpduguard default
BR1-SW01(config)# spanning-tree vlan 10,20,99 priority 4096
BR1-SW01(config)# errdisable recovery cause psecure-violation
BR1-SW01(config)# errdisable recovery cause bpduguard
BR1-SW01(config)# errdisable recovery cause dhcp-rate-limit
BR1-SW01(config)# errdisable recovery cause arp-inspection
BR1-SW01(config)# errdisable recovery interval 300
```

Verify: `show vlan brief`, `show spanning-tree summary`.

## Phase 3 - Layer 3 gateways and DHCP server

```
BR1-SW01(config)# ip routing
BR1-SW01(config)# interface Vlan10
BR1-SW01(config-if)# ip address 192.168.10.1 255.255.255.0
BR1-SW01(config-if)# no shutdown
BR1-SW01(config-if)# interface Vlan20
BR1-SW01(config-if)# ip address 192.168.20.1 255.255.255.0
BR1-SW01(config-if)# no shutdown
BR1-SW01(config-if)# interface Vlan99
BR1-SW01(config-if)# ip address 192.168.99.1 255.255.255.0
BR1-SW01(config-if)# no autostate
BR1-SW01(config-if)# no shutdown
BR1-SW01(config-if)# exit
BR1-SW01(config)# ip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.10.1 192.168.10.20
BR1-SW01(config)# ip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.20.1 192.168.20.20
BR1-SW01(config)# ip dhcp pool STAFF
BR1-SW01(dhcp-config)# network 192.168.10.0 255.255.255.0
BR1-SW01(dhcp-config)# default-router 192.168.10.1
BR1-SW01(dhcp-config)# dns-server 1.1.1.1
BR1-SW01(dhcp-config)# domain-name lab.local
BR1-SW01(dhcp-config)# lease 1
BR1-SW01(dhcp-config)# ip dhcp pool GUEST
BR1-SW01(dhcp-config)# network 192.168.20.0 255.255.255.0
BR1-SW01(dhcp-config)# default-router 192.168.20.1
BR1-SW01(dhcp-config)# dns-server 1.1.1.1
BR1-SW01(dhcp-config)# lease 0 8
BR1-SW01(dhcp-config)# exit
```

## Phase 4 - Access, management and unused ports

Apply the four `interface range` blocks from the config file:

| Range | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `Fa0/1 - 24` | STAFF-ACCESS (VLAN 10) |
| `Fa0/25 - 40` | GUEST-ACCESS (VLAN 20) |
| `Fa0/41 - 44` | MGMT-RESERVED (VLAN 99) |
| `Fa0/45 - 48, Gi0/1 - 2` | UNUSED-DISABLED (VLAN 999, shutdown) |

Example (staff ports):

```
BR1-SW01(config)# interface range FastEthernet0/1 - 24
BR1-SW01(config-if-range)# description STAFF-ACCESS
BR1-SW01(config-if-range)# switchport mode access
BR1-SW01(config-if-range)# switchport access vlan 10
BR1-SW01(config-if-range)# switchport nonegotiate
BR1-SW01(config-if-range)# switchport port-security
BR1-SW01(config-if-range)# switchport port-security maximum 1
BR1-SW01(config-if-range)# switchport port-security violation shutdown
BR1-SW01(config-if-range)# switchport port-security mac-address sticky
BR1-SW01(config-if-range)# storm-control broadcast level 20.00
BR1-SW01(config-if-range)# spanning-tree portfast
BR1-SW01(config-if-range)# spanning-tree bpduguard enable
BR1-SW01(config-if-range)# no cdp enable
```

Verify: `show interfaces status`, `show port-security`, `show running-config interface Fa0/1`.

## Phase 5 - DHCP snooping and Dynamic ARP Inspection

```
BR1-SW01(config)# no ip dhcp snooping information option
BR1-SW01(config)# ip dhcp snooping vlan 10,20
BR1-SW01(config)# ip dhcp snooping database flash:dhcp-snooping.db
BR1-SW01(config)# ip dhcp snooping
BR1-SW01(config)# ip arp inspection vlan 10,20
BR1-SW01(config)# ip arp inspection validate src-mac dst-mac ip
```

Per-port rate limit (inside the access `interface range` blocks): `ip dhcp snooping limit rate 15`.

Verify: `show ip dhcp snooping`, `show ip dhcp snooping binding`, `show ip arp inspection vlan 10,20`.

## Phase 6 - ACLs and management plane hardening

```
BR1-SW01(config)# ip access-list standard MGMT-ACCESS
BR1-SW01(config-std-nacl)# permit 192.168.10.0 0.0.0.255
BR1-SW01(config-std-nacl)# permit 192.168.99.0 0.0.0.255
BR1-SW01(config-std-nacl)# deny any log
BR1-SW01(config-std-nacl)# exit
BR1-SW01(config)# ip access-list extended GUEST-IN
BR1-SW01(config-ext-nacl)# permit udp any eq bootpc any eq bootps
BR1-SW01(config-ext-nacl)# permit icmp 192.168.20.0 0.0.0.255 host 192.168.20.1 echo
BR1-SW01(config-ext-nacl)# deny ip 192.168.20.0 0.0.0.255 192.168.10.0 0.0.0.255 log
BR1-SW01(config-ext-nacl)# deny ip 192.168.20.0 0.0.0.255 192.168.99.0 0.0.0.255 log
BR1-SW01(config-ext-nacl)# deny ip any 10.0.0.0 0.255.255.255
BR1-SW01(config-ext-nacl)# deny ip any 172.16.0.0 0.15.255.255
BR1-SW01(config-ext-nacl)# deny ip any 192.168.0.0 0.0.255.255
BR1-SW01(config-ext-nacl)# permit ip any any
BR1-SW01(config-ext-nacl)# exit
BR1-SW01(config)# interface Vlan20
BR1-SW01(config-if)# ip access-group GUEST-IN in
BR1-SW01(config-if)# exit
```

Generate the SSH key and lock down the lines:

```
BR1-SW01(config)# crypto key generate rsa modulus 2048
BR1-SW01(config)# ip ssh version 2
BR1-SW01(config)# ip ssh time-out 60
BR1-SW01(config)# ip ssh authentication-retries 3
BR1-SW01(config)# no ip http server
BR1-SW01(config)# no ip http secure-server
BR1-SW01(config)# line con 0
BR1-SW01(config-line)# login local
BR1-SW01(config-line)# exec-timeout 10 0
BR1-SW01(config-line)# logging synchronous
BR1-SW01(config-line)# line vty 0 15
BR1-SW01(config-line)# login local
BR1-SW01(config-line)# transport input ssh
BR1-SW01(config-line)# access-class MGMT-ACCESS in
BR1-SW01(config-line)# exec-timeout 10 0
BR1-SW01(config-line)# exit
```

Add the MOTD banner, logging settings and remaining service hardening from the config file.

## Phase 7 - Connect hosts, save and back up

1. Connect **PC-A** to `Fa0/1` and **PC-B** to `Fa0/25` (see [PC setup](03-pc-setup.md)).
2. Save: `copy running-config startup-config`
3. Back up the sanitised config to the repo (see "Sanitising" below).

### Sanitising a config before committing

Do **not** commit a raw `show running-config`. It contains secret hashes, sticky MAC addresses and your real device identifiers. Replace those with placeholders (`CHANGE_ME_*`) and remove the `switchport port-security mac-address sticky <mac>` lines before pushing.
